course: dictionary
lesson: 14385
title: Who started it?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An originator is the person who first thought of something, made it or started it. Originator is a formal word, so you will meet it in history books, science reports and the news. «Mia was the originator of the new playground game.» That means Mia was the first person to think of the game.
explain: Look for the clue word first and last. Someone who came later and joined in is not the originator. «The originator of the rumour was a boy in Year 5, not the girl who repeated it.» The first person to start the rumour is the originator, and the people who passed it on are not.
explain: You can check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The originator of the idea was our teacher» can become «The person who first had the idea was our teacher», and it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An originator is the person who first thought of, made or started something.
fact: Originator is a noun, so you can say an originator or originators.
fact: «The originator of the idea» means the person who first had the idea.
fact: «The originator of the rumour» means the person who first started the rumour, not the people who repeated it.
fact: Originator is a formal word, used most often in history, science and the news.
exercise: «Mia was the originator of the new playground game.» Who first thought of the game? | *Mia | The newspaper that wrote about it | The other children who played it | The teacher who watched them
exercise: «The originator of the rumour was never found.» What does originator mean here? | The person who wrote the newspaper story | The person who believed the rumour | *The person who first started the rumour | The person who spread the rumour last
exercise: «Tom was the originator of the joke, and everyone laughed.» Find and copy the word that names the person who first made the joke. | joke | laughed | *Tom | everyone
test: «Lena traced the originator of the rumour back to her cousin.» What does originator mean? | The last person to hear it | The person who first started it | The person who wrote the newspaper story | *The person who first started the rumour
test: Ravi says the originator of a rumour is the person who spreads it the most. Is he right? | *No, the originator is the person who first started it | Yes, the one who spreads it the most | Yes, the one who hears it first | No, the originator is the teacher
exam: What is an originator? | The person who uses something the most | The last person who joins in with something | The person who buys something new | *The person who first thought of, made or started something
